{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "updated": "2026-08-08",
  "_readme": [
    "PROVIDER surfaces. What an organisation OFFERS, on what terms.",
    "",
    "data/model-definitions.json says what a model IS. This file says who serves it and",
    "what they will actually accept. The two are never merged, because a provider's",
    "schema is not evidence about weights: fal's 5-second floor is not MiniMax H3's,",
    "Runware's 720p ceiling on Seedance 2.5 is not ByteDance's, and Runware's H3 seed",
    "is not a MiniMax capability. Each of those is recorded here, against the surface",
    "that declares it, and public/shared-model-intelligence.js reports the divergence",
    "rather than letting either side win.",
    "",
    "`surfaceId` is identity. An `offerings[].providerModelId` is that provider's own",
    "handle for the model - Runware's AIR string, fal's route - and is NEVER CineBraid",
    "identity: two providers name the same weights differently, and Runware's identifier",
    "for Nano Banana 2 is not the one Google publishes.",
    "",
    "`state` is a promise, and only `available` is one a screen may keep:",
    "  catalogued     researched and recorded; CineBraid cannot dispatch to it",
    "  adapter-ready  an adapter exists but is not wired to a route",
    "  available      a filmmaker can press Generate today",
    "",
    "A constraint that no cited source establishes is ABSENT, never guessed. An empty",
    "`constraints` block means CineBraid has established no narrowing, not that none",
    "exists."
  ],
